This repository contains code for causal hallucination mitigation in
vision-language models.

The original code (causal_core/, eval/, experiments/, scripts/) is released
under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

It bundles and/or derives from the following third-party components, which
remain under their respective upstream licenses. Please retain those licenses
and cite the original works:

  • llava/         — LLaVA-v1.5 model code, Haotian Liu et al.
                     Apache License 2.0.  https://github.com/haotian-liu/LLaVA

  • transformers/  — HuggingFace Transformers (patched to expose attention in
                     the LLaMA decode path).  Apache License 2.0.
                     https://github.com/huggingface/transformers

The decoding baselines re-implemented for comparison build on:

  • ONLY  — Wan et al., "One Layer Is Sufficient..." (TVER, single-layer
            text-enhanced branch; causal_core/models/*_sampling.py).
  • VCD   — Leng et al., CVPR 2024 (diffusion-noise contrastive decoding;
            causal_core/vcd.py).
  • M3ID  — Favero et al., 2024 (image-free contrastive decoding).
  • ASCD  — Wang et al., "ASCD: Attention-Steerable Contrastive Decoding
            for Reducing Hallucination in MLLM." The compatible LLaVA-1.5-7B
            integration is adapted from upstream commit
            70034c32edf2bcadb8aae57da2c4eaed82fab3e6 under Apache License 2.0.
            https://github.com/BroJunn/ASCD

Datasets used for calibration/evaluation (COCO, POPE, AMBER, MME, MMBench,
MMVP) are subject to their own terms and are not redistributed here.
